Here are the **production-ready Security Rules** for your Firestore database.

These rules are designed to work perfectly with the code I wrote for you. They ensure that users can only access their own private data, while still allowing the specific public features (like Collaborative Sessions and Feedback) to function correctly.

### 1. Firestore Database Rules
Copy and paste this code into your **Firebase Console > Firestore Database > Rules** tab.

```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // --- Helper Functions ---

    // Check if the user is signed in (even anonymously)
    function isAuthenticated() {
      return request.auth != null;
    }

    // Check if the user is accessing their own document
    function isOwner(userId) {
      return isAuthenticated() && request.auth.uid == userId;
    }

    // --- Collection Rules ---

    // 1. Users Collection (Private Data)
    // Contains Profile, Smart Plan, Notes, Timetables.
    // ONLY the specific user can read or write their own data.
    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if isOwner(userId);
    }

    // 2. Collaborative Sessions (Shared Data)
    // Allows anyone logged in to join a session if they have the Session Code (ID).
    // This is necessary for the "Join with Code" feature to work.
    match /sessions/{sessionId} {
      allow read, write: if isAuthenticated();
    }

    // 3. Feedback / Comments (Public Read, Auth Write)
    // Everyone can read comments (community view).
    // Only logged-in users can post or like.
    match /comments/{commentId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create: if isAuthenticated();
      allow update: if isAuthenticated(); 
    }

    // 4. Feedback Stats (Public Read, Auth Write)
    // Stores total counts of ratings/comments.
    match /feedback_stats/summary {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if isAuthenticated();
    }

    // 5. User Feedback Tracking (Private)
    // Tracks which comments a specific user has liked (to prevent double-liking).
    match /users_feedback/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if isOwner(userId);
    }
  }
}
```

